<title>POLAND: POLISH KGHM MIN INSTITUTIONAL OFFER PRICE PLN 19.5.</title>
<headline>POLISH KGHM MIN INSTITUTIONAL OFFER PRICE PLN 19.5.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish treasury ministry set the minimum price for final bids in the institutional offer of KGHM Polska Miedz SA copper giant at 19.5 zlotys and priced the retail offer at 19 zlotys, the offer's domestic manager said.</p>
<p>The earlier announced price range was 18-23 zlotys.</p>
<p>    Issuer:				KGHM Polska Miedz SA</p>
<p> Type of issue:			  existing common shares</p>
<p>Priced at (PLN):</p>
<p>    minimum instutional price	19.5	 </p>
<p>    final retail price		 19.0</p>
<p> (Previous) Pricing Range:	   18-23</p>
<p> No of Shares Offered:		 55,000,000-72,000,000</p>
<p> No of Existing Shares:		200,000,000</p>
<p> Lead Manager:			   United Bank of Switzerland</p>
<p>					     Barclays de Zoete Wedd</p>
<p> Domestic Manager:		     WBK SA brokerage</p>
<p> Lead Underwriter:		     To be announced</p>
<p> Issue Purpose:			  facilitate privatisation</p>
<p> Tranches		     No of Shares	   Subscription</p>
<p>				  Offered		  Period</p>
<p> Domestic Small-Investor  6,000,000	     June 30-July 4</p>
<p> Domestic Large-Investor 14,000,000	     June 30-July 4</p>
<p> International Tranche   35,000,000</p>
<p>  (book building)				     June 23-July 3</p>
<p>NOTES - Domestic and foreign tranches can be increased by</p>
<p>10,000,000 shares. An additional seven million shares may be</p>
<p>issued by global coordinators as GDRs.</p>
<p>- Price for the retail tranche fixed. Price for large</p>
<p>investors set as a minimum price for final bids on the base of</p>
<p>which the final strike price will be announced later. It will</p>
<p>also be the sale price in the international offer. The retail</p>
<p>offer will be allotted on July 7.</p>
<p>- The entire international tranche will be issued in global</p>
<p>depositary receipts (GDRs).</p>
<p>- Up to 15 percent of KGHM shares reserved for employees.</p>
<p>  Earnings Data (mln PLN)  1997 forecast	  1996</p>
<p> Net profit:		  286.0		    147.2</p>
<p> Operating profit:	  511.0		    390.3</p>
<p> Sales:		     3,683.0		  3,351.0</p>
<p> Group net profit:	  310.0		    148.9</p>
<p> Group operating:	   528.0		    387.3</p>
<p> Group sales:	     3,883.0		  3,527.2</p>
<p>Main Shareholders: State treasury - 100 pct of shares.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
